Defect: SMI-MISSING-IMPORT https://pysnmp.github.io/pysmi/stable/mib-defects.html#smi-missing-import

The module as published in ArubaOS 8.5.0.7 names three symbols it never
imports.

It gives wlanAPFlexRadioMode the SYNTAX ArubaFlexRadioMode and
wlanAPDual5GMode the SYNTAX ArubaDual5GMode. ARUBA-TC defines both
textual conventions, and the clause already imports nineteen others from
it. Without them the module does not compile: both objects have an
unknown parent type.

It also uses Gauge32 as a SYNTAX throughout the statistics tables
without naming it in the SNMPv2-SMI group.

The repair adds the two names to the existing FROM ARUBA-TC group and
Gauge32 to the existing FROM SNMPv2-SMI group.

Aruba serves its MIBs behind a support login, so this module has no
entry in mib-sources.json and nothing re-fetches the text under this
patch. The baseline is aruba-wlan.my from aruba-mibs_8.5.0.7_74786.

--- a/WLSX-WLAN-MIB
+++ b/WLSX-WLAN-MIB
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
        Unsigned32,
 	   Counter32,
 	   IpAddress,
+	   Gauge32,
 	   NOTIFICATION-TYPE
            FROM SNMPv2-SMI
 
@@ -48,7 +49,9 @@
        ArubaMeshRole,
 	   ArubaHTMode,
 	   ArubaPortSpeed,
-	   ArubaHTExtChannel
+	   ArubaHTExtChannel,
+	   ArubaFlexRadioMode,
+	   ArubaDual5GMode
 	   		FROM ARUBA-TC
 
        OBJECT-GROUP
